# Auth and transport

Do not disable, bypass, or weaken authentication or authorization checks.

Do not disable TLS, HTTPS, certificate validation, or encryption at rest without explicit user instruction.

Do not add `skipAuth`, `insecure: true`, `NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0`, or equivalent without explicit approval.

Prefer fail-closed defaults. Expose only the endpoints and data the task requires (least privilege).
